WEBVTT

00:00:00.730 --> 00:00:03.270
Come on, run!

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:06.460
Summer camp is just beginning!

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:10.780
Okay, that's it for morning training.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:12.320
Let's hit the showers.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.200
<b>Men</b>

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:15.820
<b>Women</b>

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.540
Let's make today another good day!

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:58.010
First, we'll get on the wrapped 
train on the Kashima Line,

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:02.820
and we'll check out the outlet 
gallery and the Aqua Tower,

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:04.780
and we'll put up our ita-wishing 
plaques at the shrine.

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:08.530
We need to visit the udon shop that Tildama II crashed into in Urban Warfare,

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:12.060
and check to see if there's still
a blue seat at the Seasider Hotel.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:14.530
I want to see the victory 
flag in person, too.

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:18.530
You mean that legendary one that 
a firetruck raised at a parade.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:20.990
We have to be sure to 
find some good food, too.

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:23.280
Hamburg steaks with school
crests and kushikatsu.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:25.340
Anmitsu is a must, too.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:28.750
Let's be sure to get the ankou 
manju before it gets sold out.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.780
Looks like your studying 
is paying off, Minoa.

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:32.290
Yup.

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:35.700
I looked up a lot of 
information on the meccas.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:40.980
There are around 3,000 
anime meccas across Japan.

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:43.930
Oarai, Chichibu, and...

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:48.060
Sayama and Kamakura, and 
Onomichi and the Hida region.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.540
Due to the anime boom,

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:54.610
<b>Oarai</b>

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:54.680
many local governments and shopping districts cooperate proactively, too.

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:56.580
That's amazing.

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:59.610
<b>Chichibu</b>

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:00.180
But why do people travel to the meccas?

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:15.380
<b>Sayama</b>

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:02.790
You can have fun pretending 
you're one of the characters,

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:07.350
or you can revel in the amazement of being 
at the site of a special scene in an anime.

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:10.510
It's also entertaining to play 
detective and think about

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:13.920
why a scene doesn't look 
exactly like the location.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.310
I see.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:20.800
<b>Kamakura</b>

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:18.810
You get to hear the voice actors 
say lines exclusively

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:20.660
for the meccas and buy merchandise.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:28.020
<b>Onomichi</b>

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:26.280
You can talk to other fans or 
ask a local where a rare banner is.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:27.990
You can make new friends, too.

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:34.440
<b>Hida</b>

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:30.670
You can use smartphone apps, too.

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:34.220
You can look at maps or take 
photos with characters.

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:36.530
I'm installing that, too.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:40.520
It's easy to get exited, but it's 
important to mind your manners.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:41.570
Roger that.

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:43.220
This app's amazing.

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:44.240
It is.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:45.320
Right?

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:47.330
I never knew about this app.

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:51.420
Would you like some?

00:03:59.060 --> 00:03:59.960
Sorry.

00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:01.880
Are you—

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:04.960
What's wrong? You're sweating like mad.

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:10.220
This isn't my genre!

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:14.140
Zetoro! Zetoro, are you here?!

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:20.050
Apple, otherwise known as Margrave
Mijareabatgolt has run off.

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:30.420
Hey, Musashisakai-senpai...

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:36.040
Actually, never mind.

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:38.710
She opens a conversation 
before promptly ending it,

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:42.550
her long eyelashes fluttering 
with timidity and hesitation.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:45.550
Her silhouette vanishes, 
melting into the sunset.

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:51.450
Could this be foreshadowing of a central 
development in the narrative yet to come?

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:55.450
Hey, that looked promising.

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:56.610
In-club romance, huh?

00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:58.820
You're more than welcome.

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:01.570
In-club romance? What are you talking about?

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:03.720
No way... Kouenji?

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:05.650
For me?

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:07.180
<i>Calm down.</i>

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:09.670
<i>Calm down, Musashisakai Kai.</i>

00:05:09.670 --> 00:05:12.730
<i>Analyze the situation carefully.</i>

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:14.660
Kaikai-senpai.

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:18.110
What's wrong? You just darted away.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:25.340
My brain is currently executing Emergency Order 999, the heartless seal.

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:27.560
To use the language of the commoners,

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:30.850
I am currently investigating 
the conspiracy known as "love."

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:32.600
Leave me be!

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:34.120
Thank goodness.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:36.310
You're still the usual Kaikai-senpai.

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:39.030
<i>Wait, something's not right.</i>

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:40.730
<i>He hasn't done his usual...</i>

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:42.450
Musashisakai...

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:43.110
Kai!

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:45.490
Looks like you're okay.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:49.290
I can't wait for the hot springs, either.

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:53.970
Speaking of hot springs, there 
were no God rays in <i>Girls & Tank</i>.

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:57.080
Bath scenes can really influence 
how a show is perceived.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:58.870
They can't help but be careful.

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:00.370
God rays!

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:01.510
I know what those are.

00:06:01.510 --> 00:06:07.450
They're one of the mysteries of anime that 
show up on TV and vanish on the discs.

00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:09.660
I've never seen one before.

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:11.440
I can't wait to see.

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:14.640
These travel bookmarks 
are really well chosen.

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:17.780
Minoacchi did a lot of the research for us.

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:19.650
She stayed until really 
late at the club room.

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:22.670
Nah, I'm still a newbie.

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:26.030
My friend in the track club is at 
training camp for a whole month.

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:31.410
I'm hoping to beat my own record at the camp.

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:34.160
Watch me get it done!

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:37.160
Japan's first anime minister!

00:06:37.590 --> 00:06:40.060
I hope you come visit our country.

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:42.420
What are you guys talking about?

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:47.250
We're discussing our ambitious 
goals as anime club members.

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:48.600
Wow.

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:50.430
But what do you mean by anime minister?

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:57.750
I'm not sure, but I guess it's the wish 
that anime will bring the world together.

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:58.680
What about you guys?

00:06:59.050 --> 00:07:02.010
To have a commanding knowledge 
of all the anime in existence,

00:07:02.010 --> 00:07:04.270
and store it all in here.

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:07.440
To write a light novel and have 
it become an anime one day.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:10.870
To destroy the wall between 2D and 3D.

00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:13.450
There's no reason to make 
a distinction, anyway.

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:18.660
It's amazing that you all have proper goals.

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:21.330
<i>I don't have anything.</i>

00:07:21.530 --> 00:07:24.280
Okay, let's announce our goals for today.

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:25.040
Bam!

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:26.920
<b>Girls &
Tank Tops</b>

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:26.920
<b>Concept Art</b>

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:27.600
Get through all the cuts in <i>Girls & Tank</i>!

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:28.920
That's exciting.

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:30.870
That's brutal.

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:34.470
But it's to be expected of 
a pilgrimage to the meccas.

00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:37.060
And a disc festival at the hotel.

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:39.020
Let's do this!

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:44.810
<b>Helping to Raise Children
Oarai, city of kind smiles</b>

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:48.030
Here we go, our mecca tour!

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:50.280
Let's get our first stamp!

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:58.320
Here we are.

00:07:57.160 --> 00:08:06.540
<b>Udon</b>

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:00.890
This is the shop that...

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:06.540
<b>Nekomura Head Shop</b>

00:08:00.890 --> 00:08:04.350
Rosehappy's Crubaider took Klaklara's T-34
with it and crashed into in the movie...

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:06.540
And got destroyed!

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:09.040
It's the real thing!

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:09.550
Wow!

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:11.970
I'm sorry!

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:13.090
I'm sorry!

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:15.010
Woo!

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:20.040
People are really into it.

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:21.630
I bought these.

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:24.440
That's kind of you, Minoacchi.

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:37.800
Well, you know what they say 
about poop and good fortune.

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:39.490
Come on, chin up.

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:43.180
Look, it's the same scene that Rinpomi saw.

00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:46.250
It's so pretty.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:48.670
You're right.

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:51.780
I have to enjoy the pilgrimage.

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:55.360
Look out!

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:58.300
Wait!

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:05.790
I keep screwing up.

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:07.910
Don't worry about it.

00:09:07.910 --> 00:09:10.190
Things happen when you travel.

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:12.570
Things happen?!

00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:15.470
The clumsy-girl character 
is part of your charm.

00:09:15.470 --> 00:09:16.550
Right.

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:20.360
Kaikai-senpai...

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:22.080
Don't tell me he's angry...

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:34.090
I didn't expect you to breach my barrier.

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:37.890
Do you intend to control my heart?

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:47.570
I won't let you!

00:09:47.570 --> 00:09:50.940
I shouldn't have come on the trip, should I?

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:54.370
Begone, show yourself no more!

00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:55.550
I understand.

00:09:55.550 --> 00:09:57.250
It's my fault.

00:09:57.250 --> 00:09:59.160
I'll take the next train home.

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:02.620
I don't mind you fighting the organization...

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:04.480
...but that was bad timing.

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:05.640
S-Sorry.

00:10:05.990 --> 00:10:07.340
There, there.

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:12.000
What?!

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:14.310
There's no TV.

00:10:14.310 --> 00:10:16.380
No DVD player.

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:19.010
We're going to miss <i>Yuri!!! on Nice</i>.

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:22.240
What's going to happen to our 
overnight DVD viewing party?

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:23.890
Yo, you guys are late.

00:10:24.210 --> 00:10:25.270
I've been waiting for you.

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:26.730
Gomon-sensei!

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:28.270
What is the meaning of this?!

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:30.900
Sorry about that.

00:10:31.140 --> 00:10:34.150
I couldn't get funding. 
This is the best I could find.

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:37.270
Why didn't you use the club funding, then?

00:10:37.270 --> 00:10:40.160
Who was it that used 640,000 
of club funds, again?

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:43.530
The outdoor baths are pretty nice, though.

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:45.700
They have cutting-edge massage machines, too.

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:52.620
I can't hang all of them.

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:54.060
Of course you can't.

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:55.770
Going somewhere, Minoa?

00:10:56.900 --> 00:11:00.180
N-No, I'm just going to take a bath.

00:11:06.580 --> 00:11:08.830
What am I even doing?

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:12.250
I'm ruining our club trip.

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:17.900
I guess I'll just go take a bath.

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:20.150
Outdoor Baths

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:20.150
Forest

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:25.440
One often forgets that they 
live in the Meatspace,

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:28.540
imagining the world they idolize 
in superposition with reality.

00:11:28.770 --> 00:11:31.470
As in <i>Donmachi and Aekoi</i>.

00:11:31.470 --> 00:11:35.260
The protagonist is adored by a cute girl.

00:11:35.260 --> 00:11:36.120
Indeed.

00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:38.150
Should that happen in real life,

00:11:38.150 --> 00:11:41.180
you wouldn't fully believe 
it could be happening to you.

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:44.520
You would want to know how she <i>really</i> feels.

00:11:44.520 --> 00:11:45.550
As soon as possible.

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:47.230
Immediately, if possible!

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:51.910
Oh, I'm asking for a friend.

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:56.540
So you're asking how to know 
how a girl feels about you?

00:11:57.970 --> 00:12:06.450
Well, I think girls constantly give some 
kind of hint to the person they like.

00:12:06.610 --> 00:12:07.700
Hints?

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:11.060
For example, in <i>Oresama Monogatari</i>,

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:13.880
Tsuyoo misses all of Tomato-chan's signs of love

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:16.780
because he feels certain that 
no one could ever like him.

00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:20.690
Indeed, objectively, it was 
quite an obvious sign of love.

00:12:20.690 --> 00:12:26.190
You should analyze the girl's actions with 
a clean slate, without any preconceptions.

00:12:26.190 --> 00:12:30.220
A message, a phone call, a fleeting glance...

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:33.230
With a clean slate...

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:35.230
<i>What she did earlier...</i>

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:37.900
<i>Was that a sign of love?</i>

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:42.320
<i>Was that not an accident 
but a deliberate act?</i>

00:12:43.090 --> 00:12:46.490
<i>Am I already under her spell?</i>

00:12:48.640 --> 00:12:51.190
<i>What other signs of love were there?</i>

00:12:51.190 --> 00:12:54.270
<i>Think, Musashisakai Kai!</i>

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:02.010
Do you have a minute? It's about Minoa.
It's not that I need advice, but there's something
we need to talk about. Please hear us out.
The three of us girls are headed 
to your room. See you there. ♥

00:13:01.010 --> 00:13:04.010
A heart mark!

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:09.010
<b>Kaikai Love Climax</b>

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:18.020
A heart mark!

00:13:18.710 --> 00:13:20.060
A heart mark?

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:22.290
You mean the heart mark in LINE Chat?

00:13:22.290 --> 00:13:23.530
I guess.

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:26.160
I hear girls use them pretty casually,

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:29.970
but some girls only use them 
for people they really like.

00:13:29.970 --> 00:13:32.660
It's hard to tell, because it 
depends on her personality.

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:34.160
<i>Which is it?!</i>

00:13:34.570 --> 00:13:37.100
<i>All is determined by the Shrimp's Gate.</i>

00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:41.150
<i>Is there no way to resist it?!</i>

00:13:41.540 --> 00:13:42.820
We're coming in.

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:43.590
Come in.

00:13:44.150 --> 00:13:45.850
Want me to close the gate?

00:13:45.850 --> 00:13:46.730
It's a club meeting.

00:13:46.730 --> 00:13:47.610
Oh.

00:13:47.610 --> 00:13:48.320
Right.

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:52.930
It's unusual for Minoa to be depressed.

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:54.220
I'm worried.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:58.080
I feel like we've discovered a new persona.

00:13:58.080 --> 00:14:03.340
I think Minoa-chan is trying to find 
her identity as an anime club member.

00:14:03.340 --> 00:14:04.890
Identity?

00:14:05.260 --> 00:14:07.290
She doesn't need to think about that.

00:14:07.290 --> 00:14:09.750
She just has to be herself.

00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:11.420
What would that be like?

00:14:11.420 --> 00:14:15.670
I think of her listening 
to people with a smile.

00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:20.250
But she can sometimes be surprisingly 
passionate and proactive.

00:14:20.470 --> 00:14:23.500
Yes, like the time I got 
in a fight with Miko.

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:27.260
I'd feel bad for anime if we 
rejected each other over it.

00:14:27.810 --> 00:14:30.080
She really touched my heart.

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:32.260
And her speech at the student assembly...

00:14:32.650 --> 00:14:35.770
We have lost but one club room...

00:14:36.150 --> 00:14:42.860
The audience was baffled, but her effort 
ultimately carried us to victory.

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:45.030
Even when we were bummed out about 
the club getting shut down...

00:14:45.520 --> 00:14:49.230
I want to continue this club 
with you and everyone else.

00:14:50.020 --> 00:14:52.640
She's always strong and hard-working.

00:14:53.230 --> 00:14:56.910
It's thanks to her that the Anime 
Club exists as it does now.

00:14:57.280 --> 00:15:01.220
Minoa ought to just be her usual self.

00:15:01.220 --> 00:15:02.920
I agree.

00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:05.740
She's a precious friend.

00:15:05.740 --> 00:15:10.430
We're going to support her and 
have her back, no matter what.

00:15:10.700 --> 00:15:11.520
Yeah.

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:13.930
Why don't you tell her that?

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:16.460
Right.

00:15:16.750 --> 00:15:17.460
Yeah.

00:15:17.510 --> 00:15:18.400
Yes.

00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:21.860
Minoa's been in the bath 
for a while now, though.

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:24.680
Where am I?!

00:15:24.680 --> 00:15:27.070
Where's the bath?!

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:30.070
Outdoor Baths

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:30.070
Forest

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:30.070
Let's split up and look for her.

00:15:30.970 --> 00:15:32.890
Call my cell phone if anything happens.

00:15:32.890 --> 00:15:34.580
Don't put yourselves in danger.

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:35.450
Sebas!

00:16:01.780 --> 00:16:05.820
Does Kouenji really hurgh me?

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:08.980
No! I need to focus on finding Asagaya.

00:16:09.180 --> 00:16:11.790
Still, I need to know.

00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:15.080
I've finally got it!

00:16:15.080 --> 00:16:21.500
Reading it vertically, it 
says "I can't tell you <3"

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:24.880
This heart is no doubt...

00:16:28.450 --> 00:16:30.160
Kai-senpai...

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:31.430
Miko...

00:16:31.430 --> 00:16:34.600
It's the beginning of our rainbow days.

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:39.490
What destructive power!

00:16:39.490 --> 00:16:43.930
Forgive me, Kouenji, I've just 
now understood how you feel.

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:46.450
It was true!

00:16:46.450 --> 00:16:48.040
I want to meet you now!

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:51.030
But first, I must find Asagaya.

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:53.360
<i>Duty or love?</i>

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:55.910
<i>We are just like a yin yang of fate.</i>

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:57.170
<i>We shall someday marry.</i>

00:16:57.170 --> 00:17:00.040
<i>But first, I must part the 
darkness and go forth.</i>

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:03.040
<i>Part </i>everything<i>!</i>

00:17:10.790 --> 00:17:12.840
Are you all right, little kitten?

00:17:13.780 --> 00:17:15.590
Nakano-senpai!

00:17:18.770 --> 00:17:20.760
Are you having fun in the club?

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:22.960
Yes, of course.

00:17:22.960 --> 00:17:27.510
I feel like anime's opened 
up a whole new world for me.

00:17:27.510 --> 00:17:31.620
I couldn't talk with Arisu-chan or 
Miko-chan before, but now we're friends.

00:17:31.620 --> 00:17:37.110
Of course, I'm glad I met you and 
Kaikai-senpai and Erika-senpai.

00:17:37.390 --> 00:17:38.610
Yeah?

00:17:38.610 --> 00:17:39.620
But...

00:17:39.900 --> 00:17:42.620
I'm screwing up our trip.

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:44.540
I kind of hate myself.

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:48.110
We were actually just 
having a Minoa discussion.

00:17:48.110 --> 00:17:49.580
A Minoa discussion?

00:17:50.030 --> 00:17:53.380
We were talking about you.

00:17:53.720 --> 00:17:56.660
What about me?

00:17:56.660 --> 00:17:57.880
Do you want to know?

00:17:58.810 --> 00:17:59.630
It's a secret.

00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:01.520
Come on!

00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:03.890
I can say this for certain, though:

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:07.140
that everyone loves you.

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:10.280
Minoa!

00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:11.680
See?

00:18:11.680 --> 00:18:16.090
You can tell from the looks on 
their faces that I'm not lying.

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:18.990
Minoa!

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:23.940
Thank goodness.

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:25.480
We were worried about you.

00:18:25.690 --> 00:18:26.760
Jeez...

00:18:27.020 --> 00:18:27.950
You idiot!

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:29.230
You idiot!

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:31.540
I'm sorry.

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:33.120
Thanks.

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:36.000
Where's Kaikai, though?

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:38.130
Did he get lost, too?

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:39.710
We have to find him soon.

00:18:41.310 --> 00:18:43.790
What is that voice?

00:18:44.190 --> 00:18:46.310
Could it be paranormal activity?

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:52.820
I-Is that Kaikai-senpai?!

00:18:52.820 --> 00:18:55.570
Is he n-naked?!

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:04.950
It's all right, guys.

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:08.460
Thank goodness, you can't see it.

00:19:10.180 --> 00:19:13.810
Are these the so-called "God rays"?

00:19:13.810 --> 00:19:17.020
I finally get to see them in person.

00:19:17.020 --> 00:19:18.320
I'm awestruck.

00:19:18.320 --> 00:19:19.660
What are you talking about?

00:19:19.660 --> 00:19:22.190
Those aren't anime God rays.

00:19:22.190 --> 00:19:23.990
Those are real God rays!

00:19:25.150 --> 00:19:27.340
Thank goodness you're safe.

00:19:27.340 --> 00:19:28.600
Lights off.

00:19:45.970 --> 00:19:47.430
Boomshakalaka.

00:19:47.430 --> 00:19:49.080
I see.

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:51.870
So that's what "God rays" are.

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:54.880
I'm a little smarter now.

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:59.880
Minoa, no matter what, you're a 
precious member of the anime club.

00:20:01.190 --> 00:20:02.890
Don't forget that.

00:20:07.330 --> 00:20:08.090
Okay.

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:13.900
Musashisakai-senpai.

00:20:15.070 --> 00:20:18.150
There's something I want 
to talk to you about.

00:20:19.460 --> 00:20:24.160
I wanted to talk, too.

00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:26.910
Okay, you go first, Senpai.

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:32.160
I, thou, I mean, thine...

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:40.670
I like you!

00:20:44.490 --> 00:20:46.370
I knew it.

00:20:46.770 --> 00:20:50.030
You're in love with Nakano-senpai!

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:53.190
You're such a cute couple!

00:20:56.140 --> 00:20:59.050
When you were sitting facing 
each other in the train,

00:20:59.050 --> 00:21:03.880
you were all restless and looking 
at the ground and turning red.

00:21:03.880 --> 00:21:05.330
I thought, "Could it be?"

00:21:05.330 --> 00:21:07.700
And it hit me!

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:09.730
No, that's, uh...

00:21:09.730 --> 00:21:12.330
I think you're making a mistake.

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:14.120
Oh, it's okay.

00:21:14.610 --> 00:21:16.070
Musanaka?

00:21:16.070 --> 00:21:17.350
Nakamusa!

00:21:17.350 --> 00:21:19.840
Let's build a church here!

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:25.600
I'm only really interested in 2D, 
but for you two, I'm totally in.

00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:32.220
2D...

00:21:32.530 --> 00:21:37.110
Um, then, what were you 
about to say last night?

00:21:37.110 --> 00:21:38.090
Last night?

00:21:39.630 --> 00:21:41.030
I don't remember.

00:21:42.150 --> 00:21:45.590
I'm just way too shocked about you guys.

00:21:47.220 --> 00:21:48.810
Want to hit the baths again?

00:21:48.810 --> 00:21:49.500
Yeah.

00:23:27.650 --> 00:23:30.640
Next episode, we learn of 
the unthinkable secret.

00:23:30.640 --> 00:23:33.130
Don't think too hard about text 
messages or vertical text.

00:23:33.130 --> 00:23:37.470
Oh, and whoever invented the heart mark...

00:23:37.470 --> 00:23:39.860
Come see me behind the tank!
